EmuLoader ReLoaded License

EmuLoader ReLoaded is a community continuation of EmuLoader, originally created by Ciro Alfredo
Consentino (1974-2021). Ported from his Emuloader v8.9.4.

EmuLoader was released by its author as freeware and as an open source project, on these terms:
"It can be distributed freely. It cannot be sold. It cannot be used for commercial purposes."
EmuLoader ReLoaded is based on EmuLoader's source code, and keeps those terms.

EmuLoader: copyright Ciro Alfredo Consentino.
EmuLoader ReLoaded's own changes and additions: copyright 2026 the EmuLoader ReLoaded contributors.

Permission is granted, free of charge, to anyone who obtains EmuLoader ReLoaded (the program, its
source code and its documentation) to use it, copy it and share it, and to change it and share
the changed version, on these conditions:

1. Free of charge. EmuLoader ReLoaded, and any version changed from it, may not be sold, may not
   be part of anything that is sold, and may not be used for commercial purposes. A fee for the
   service of copying it is a sale.

2. The credits stay. Every copy, changed or not, keeps this license, the credit to Ciro Alfredo
   Consentino as EmuLoader's creator, and the credit to EmuLoader ReLoaded.

3. Changed versions say so. A changed version must say that it was changed, and must not be
   presented as an official release of EmuLoader ReLoaded.

4. Changed versions stay open. Whoever shares a changed version must make its source code
   available to the people who receive it, on these same terms.

5. The other parts keep their own licenses. EmuLoader ReLoaded includes and uses software by
   others, each under its own license (Qt, miniz, the LZMA SDK, the Press Start 2P font and the
   video player's libmpv and FFmpeg). Their licenses are in the "licenses" folder of the program,
   and in the "third_party" and "resources" folders of the source code. This license doesn't
   change theirs.

No warranty. EmuLoader ReLoaded is provided as it is, without any warranty of any kind, express
or implied. Its authors are not responsible for any loss of data, damage to a computer or other
harm caused by using it, or by not being able to use it.
